        {
          "id": "beat_purpose_01",
          "title": "Two sources, one conversation",
          "narration": "Bunbun is a comment and discussion service built on the AT Protocol. Buns and threads are persisted as ATProto records, and a local index serves reads alongside the PDS source of truth. The index is a read model and a cache; it is never the place where a conversation truly lives.",
          "durationMs": 32000,
          "anchors": [
            {
              "id": "anchor_readme_overview",
              "path": "README.md",
              "lines": {
                "start": 3,
                "end": 3
              },
              "label": "What Bunbun is"
            }
          ],
          "stage": {
            "anchorIds": ["anchor_readme_overview"],
            "diagramId": "diagram_sources",
            "nodeIds": ["node_pds", "node_index"],
            "edgeIds": ["edge_pds_index", "edge_api_index"]
          },
          "suggestedQuestions": [
            "Why keep a local index if the PDS is the source of truth?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "beat_purpose_02",
          "title": "Three application surfaces",
          "narration": "The repository is a pnpm workspace with three application surfaces. apps/api is the NestJS service, apps/web is the browser island bundle served same-origin, and apps/browser-acceptance is an opt-in Playwright tier. docs and plans hold the project's memory.",
          "durationMs": 30000,
          "anchors": [
            {
              "id": "anchor_readme_layout",
