          }
        },
        {
          "id": "beat_write_04",
          "title": "One writer invalidates the cache",
          "narration": "IndexWriter is the single write path for the local index. Each write invalidates the affected cache shape before the write resolves, so a reader never sees a stale shape after a successful mutation. Comments, threads, and tags all ride the same writer, which is how invalidation stays honest across features.",
