        {
          "id": "beat_index_01",
          "title": "The worker owns the writes",
          "narration": "The sync worker runs in its own thread with its own Prisma client. It owns the IndexWriter, posts invalidation events to the main process, and runs the reconcilers. That is why the worker never touches the main process's read-through cache: it has no request context and no business seeing another thread's memory.",
          "durationMs": 40000,
          "anchors": [
            {
